Z||000002||Gokart||04-23-2000||07:37 AM||||Noticed he started out the bidding low so I'm curious how much the reserve is? With the amount of time these auctions last if it was over $5000.00 he should've started the bidding at $3500.00 unless he's practically giving it away!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||04-23-2000||10:55 AM||||The reason the starting bid is low is Ebay's pricing. If he doesn't sell it, (gets to his reserve) he still has to pay Ebay for the ad.<BR>I think it's 1% for cars. So if he had the starting bid at $5000 he'd have to pay $50 to place the ad, But at $1000 it would only be $10. That is why you see a lot of low starting bids with high reserves.||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||04-23-2000||11:31 AM||||i JUST HOPE THE SELLER IS NOT ONE WHO THINKS THE 87 MODELS ARE REALLY EVER GOING TO HAVE STRONG CHANCE OF EVER BEING A TRUE COLLECTABLE. THE CAR IS GREAT AND HE SHOULD BE COMPENSATED BUT SOME THESE PRICES I SEE FOR 87 AND 86 MODELS JUST BLOWS MY MIND. NOW REALISTICLY ...THERE WAS A DEALERSHIP DOWN IN SOUTH FL THAT HAD AN 87 WITH 30,000 MILES ON IT ASKING 4995.00 MINT CONDITION/ OF COURSE ! I MISSED OUT ON THAT ONE. IT WAS GONE BY FIRST DAY. FOR THIS CAR I COULD SEE GETTING ALITTLE MORE SAY 5 OR 6 BUT I SAW ONE FOR 10,000.00!!!! UHHH WITH 50,000 MILES/ THE GUY WOULD NOT BUDGE ...I TRIED TO EXPLAIN TO HIM THAT IT REALLY WAS THE 88'S BUT HE WOULD NOT BUDGE! THE CAR WAS POSTED FOREVER !!!!I THINK FINALLY CAME DOWN. OOOOPS SORRY WAS THAT A RAMBLE !!!????? YEAH THINK IT WAS ! ||||reg||1
Z||000005||LarryB||04-24-2000||12:23 AM||||The best thing you can do is vote with your wallet, if the price is out of line just pass, if the guy managed to find a sucker just tip your hat and move on.<P>I've looked at a couple of Fieros recently (I'm considering getting a 3rd Fiero) and some guys act like they were selling licenses to print money, not cars that needed major to near-complete restoration. In one instance there's a sad story prompting the sale and I wish all of these people luck but some of them are dreamers. <BR>||||reg||1
